IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-actors`
IMPORT `ccc30-forms-warrants`

-- ccc30-tests-forms-warrants.l4 -- tests for ccc30-forms-warrants.l4 (Forms 7, 7.1, 8, 16, 16.1 and 19 to 23, raw lines 18015-18072, 18346-18374 and 18403-18462).
-- Every expected value is written by hand from the words of the Form named in the comment beside it, never from the module's output.
-- A #TRACE prints its outcome and no assertion line: the expected outcome is written above each trace and read by eye.

-- A hand-written constructor, so that the tests do not call the module's own helper.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      ss IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Provision of the Code`
`forms 7 to 23 test provision` MEANS `Provision of the Code` WITH `section` IS n, `subsection` IS ss

§ `Tests -- Form 7, the grounds and the sections the Form cites for each`

-- "[507(4), 512(1)]"
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (a)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 507 "(4)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512 "(1)")
-- "[512(2)]" for each of (b), (c) and (d)
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (b)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512 "(2)")
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (c)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512 "(2)")
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (d)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512 "(2)")
-- "[520(5), 521(5)]"
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (e)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 520 "(5)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 521 "(5)")
-- "[512.3]" for each of (f) and (g)
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (f)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512.3 "")
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (g)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512.3 "")
-- "[512.1, 512.2]"
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (h)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512.1 "", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 512.2 "")
-- "[597]"
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (i)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 597 "")
-- "(j) (if none of the above applies, reproduce the provisions of the statute that authorize this warrant)": the Form cites none; not covered
#ASSERT `form 7 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 7 ground (j)` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- Form 7, entry into the dwelling-house`

-- box checked, and the officer has, immediately before entering, reasonable grounds to believe the person is present
#ASSERT `form 7 the officer may enter the dwelling-house to arrest the accused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- box checked, but without that belief: "you may not enter the dwelling-house unless you have, immediately before entering ..., reasonable grounds to believe"
#ASSERT `form 7 the officer may enter the dwelling-house to arrest the accused` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- box not checked: the grant "this warrant is also issued to authorize you to enter the dwelling-house" is not in the warrant: outside the grant's words, not an express no (fork F-V), belief or not
#ASSERT `form 7 the officer may enter the dwelling-house to arrest the accused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 7 the officer may enter the dwelling-house to arrest the accused` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- "you are ordered ... to immediately arrest the accused and to bring them before (state court, judge or justice)": the officers arrest and bring them -> FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 7 the peace officers must arrest the accused and bring them before the court, judge or justice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a peace officer` DOES `form 7 arrests the accused and brings them before the court, judge or justice named in the warrant` AT 1

§ `Tests -- Form 7.1, the warrant to enter a dwelling-house`

-- ground (b): "paragraph 495(1)(a) or (b) or section 672.91"
#ASSERT `form 7.1 the sections the Form names in the ground` `form 7.1 ground (b)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 495 "(1)(a)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 495 "(1)(b)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 672.91 "")
-- grounds (a) and (c) name no section of this Act ("this or any other Act of Parliament"; "an Act of Parliament, other than this Act")
#ASSERT `form 7.1 the sections the Form names in the ground` `form 7.1 ground (a)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 7.1 the sections the Form names in the ground` `form 7.1 ground (c)` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "This warrant is issued to authorize you to enter the dwelling-house for the purpose of arresting or apprehending the person."
#ASSERT `form 7.1 the warrant authorizes the officer to enter the dwelling-house` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 7.1 the warrant authorizes the officer to enter the dwelling-house` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 7.1 the warrant authorizes the officer to enter the dwelling-house` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 7.1 the warrant authorizes the officer to enter the dwelling-house` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- Form 8, the warrant for committal`

#ASSERT `form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 8 ground (a)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 515 "(5)")
-- "[519(1), 520(9), 521(10), 524(8), 525(6)]"
#ASSERT `form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 8 ground (b)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 519 "(1)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 520 "(9)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 521 "(10)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 524 "(8)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 525 "(6)")
#ASSERT `form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 8 ground (c)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 521 "")
-- "[515(10), 523.1(3), 524(3), (4) and (6.2)]": the bare (4) and (6.2) belong to section 524
#ASSERT `form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 8 ground (d)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 515 "(10)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 523.1 "(3)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 524 "(3)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 524 "(4)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 524 "(6.2)")
#ASSERT `form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 8 ground (e)` EQUALS JUST (LIST `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 515 "(10)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 524 "(3)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 524 "(4)", `forms 7 to 23 test provision` 524 "(6.2)")
#ASSERT `form 8 the sections the Form cites for the ground` `form 8 ground (f)` EQUALS NOTHING

-- "keep them safely there until they are delivered by due course of law"
#ASSERT `form 8 the keeper is to keep the accused in custody in the prison` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 8 the keeper is to keep the accused in custody in the prison` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "You are ordered to receive the accused in your custody in this prison": the keeper receives the accused -> FULFILLED.
#TRACE `form 8 the keeper must receive the accused into custody` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the keeper of a prison` DOES `form 8 receives the accused into custody in the prison` AT 1

§ `Tests -- Form 16, the subpoena to a witness`

-- "command you to attend ... to give evidence": 7 days until the day set out. Attending at day 5 or at day 7 (the last day) -> FULFILLED; not attending by day 8 -> BREACH.
#TRACE `form 16 the witness must attend and give evidence` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a witness` DOES `form 16 attends before the court or justice, gives evidence and brings the things specified` AT 5

#TRACE `form 16 the witness must attend and give evidence` 7 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a witness` DOES `form 16 attends before the court or justice, gives evidence and brings the things specified` AT 7

#TRACE `form 16 the witness must attend and give evidence` 7 AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8

§ `Tests -- Form 16.1, the take note paragraphs`

-- "You are only required to bring the things specified above to the court on the date and at the time indicated"
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is required to` `form 16.1 bring the things specified to the court on the date and at the time indicated` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "you are not required to provide the things specified to any person or to discuss their contents with any person unless and until ordered by the court to do so"
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is required to` `form 16.1 provide the things specified to a person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is required to` `form 16.1 discuss the contents of the things specified with a person` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- once the court has ordered it, the exception is met and the sentence says no more (NOTES.md F-B)
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is required to` `form 16.1 provide the things specified to a person` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is required to` `form 16.1 discuss the contents of the things specified with a person` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "only required to bring": anything else is not required
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is required to` `form 16.1 do anything else` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is required to` `form 16.1 do anything else` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- "If anything specified above is a record or therapeutic record ..., it may be subject to a determination by the court"
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the thing may be subject to a determination by the court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the thing may be subject to a determination by the court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "the production of which is governed by sections 278.1 to 278.19 ..., this subpoena must be accompanied by a copy of an application ..., and you will have an opportunity to make submissions"
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the subpoena must be accompanied by a copy of the application made under section 278.12` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the subpoena must be accompanied by a copy of the application made under section 278.12` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness will have an opportunity to make submissions to the court concerning the production` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness will have an opportunity to make submissions to the court concerning the production` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "you are not required to bring it with you until a determination is made": the bar is JUST TRUE before the determination and JUST FALSE after it
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is not yet required to bring the record or therapeutic record` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is not yet required to bring the record or therapeutic record` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- a thing outside sections 278.1 to 278.19 is outside the sentence
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is not yet required to bring the record or therapeutic record` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 the witness is not yet required to bring the record or therapeutic record` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The definition of record quoted from section 278.1: personal information with a reasonable expectation of privacy; includes the listed kinds; excludes records made by the investigators or prosecutors
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` TRUE `form 16.1 none of those kinds` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 a medical record` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 an education record` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 an employment record` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 a child welfare record` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 an adoption record` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 a social services record` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 a personal journal or diary` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 a record containing personal information the production or disclosure of which is protected by any other Act of Parliament or a provincial legislature` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- none of the means limb and none of the includes list: "record means"
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 none of those kinds` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "but does not include records made by persons responsible for the investigation or prosecution of the offence"
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` TRUE `form 16.1 none of those kinds` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a record` FALSE `form 16.1 a medical record` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The definition of therapeutic record quoted from section 278.1: produced in the course of psychiatric treatment or any therapy or counselling, provided by an entitled health care professional
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a therapeutic record` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a therapeutic record` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a therapeutic record` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 16.1 as quoted from section 278.1 the thing is a therapeutic record` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Tests -- Forms 19 to 23, what the keeper is to do`

-- Form 19: "until the day when that person’s remand expires ... unless you are otherwise directed before that time"
#ASSERT `form 19 the keeper is to keep the person safely in custody` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 19 the keeper is to keep the person safely in custody` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 19 the keeper is to keep the person safely in custody` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 19 the keeper is to keep the person safely in custody` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Form 20: "for the term of days, unless they sooner consent to do what was required of them"
#ASSERT `form 20 the keeper is to keep the witness safely in custody` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 20 the keeper is to keep the witness safely in custody` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 20 the keeper is to keep the witness safely in custody` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 20 the keeper is to keep the witness safely in custody` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Form 21: "unless, if a term of imprisonment was imposed only in default of payment of a fine or costs, those amounts and the costs and charges ... are paid sooner"
#ASSERT `form 21 the keeper is to imprison the offender for the term of imprisonment` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 21 the keeper is to imprison the offender for the term of imprisonment` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a term not imposed only in default of payment: the "unless" does not operate, whatever has been paid
#ASSERT `form 21 the keeper is to imprison the offender for the term of imprisonment` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 21 the keeper is to imprison the offender for the term of imprisonment` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Form 22: "for the term of , unless the amounts and the costs and charges ... are sooner paid"
#ASSERT `form 22 the keeper is to keep the defendant safely in custody` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 22 the keeper is to keep the defendant safely in custody` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 22 the keeper is to keep the defendant safely in custody` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Form 23: "until he enters into a recognizance as aforesaid or until he is discharged in due course of law"
#ASSERT `form 23 the keeper is to imprison the accused` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `form 23 the keeper is to imprison the accused` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 23 the keeper is to imprison the accused` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `form 23 the keeper is to imprison the accused` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
